  "body": "Separate user post script evaluation from the prelude and add execution limits, the blank template, and built-in sample streams in `crates/post`.\n\n## Scope\n\n1. Update `Script::load` (`crates/post/src/post/js.rs`) to evaluate `PRELUDE`, `ROTARY_CAP`, and `EXPLAIN_JS` before evaluating user `.cps` source in a second call. Return exact 1-based user line and column numbers in script errors.\n2. Apply `boa_engine::RuntimeLimits` (`set_loop_iteration_limit`, `set_recursion_limit`, `set_stack_size_limit`) before running user scripts so endless loops stop cleanly on desktop and `wasm32`. Cap maximum output lines per run.\n3. Define the clean-room Blank Template constant (`description`, `vendor`, `legal`, `extension`, `capabilities = 1`, `serves = [\"mill\"]`, `programUnits = \"mm\"`, empty hooks `onOpen` through `onClose`) using public RS-274 / ISO 6983 conventions only.\n4. Expose embedded preview sample `.cnc` streams built from representative committed goldens in `crates/app/tests/golden/` (dressed with setup, operation, tool, spindle, and cycle feed records like `common::legacy_program::as_program`) and a default VMC machine JSON.\n\n## Rules\n\n- Keep all shipped post outputs deterministic and byte-identical.\n- Use only public G-code standards and existing project files (Clean-Room Protocol).\n\n## Done means\n\n- Tests verify exact 1-based line numbers on syntax errors and runtime exceptions in user `.cps` code.\n- Tests verify that `while (true) {}` aborts cleanly with a clear error message.\n- Tests verify that the Blank Template compiles and posts zero lines with zero warnings on basic milling samples.\n- Tests verify that every built-in sample stream posts cleanly through `fanuc.cps` and `mazak.cps`.\n\nPart of #2050\n",
